   "id": "us-rebound-huang-nvidia",
   "group": "United States",
   "headline": "US stocks surge as Nvidia reinstates Huang as chief executive",
   "when": "Mon 23 Nov · US session",
   "what": "The S&P 500 closed up 4.73% at 7,237.17 and the Nasdaq up 6.51% at 24,089.56. Nvidia's board put Jensen Huang back as CEO and director, effective immediately, its filing shows. Nvidia shares rose about 31%. Chip stocks led and the 10-year Treasury yield was 4.92%, up 1 basis point. The Nasdaq had fallen 10.4% the week before.",
   "why": "Your US exposure is mainly index funds and large tech names, so the rebound lifts them. Fund NAVs for ES-US500RMF and K-USA-A(D) still show 19 Nov prices this morning. The dashboard refreshes again at 11:30. After a move this size, expect large swings to continue.",
